{{Quote|It was the one place on all of Lothal where you felt the Empire wasn't welcome.|Ezra Bridger, about Old Jho's Pit Stop|<ref name="The Occupation" />}}
'''Old Jho's Pit Stop''' was a repair facility and [[cantina]] in the outpost [[Jhothal]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. It was named after its owner, an [[Ithorian]] named [[Jho]]. The [[Spectres|crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]'' were regulars, and would sometimes use the cantina as safe harbor.

==Description==
One of the few places where [[Lothal]]'s old frontier spirit survived,<ref name="Lothal">{{Databank|lothal|Lothal}}</ref> Old Jho's Pit Stop was a remote repair facility<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger">''[[Ezra's Duel with Danger]]''</ref> and [[Hangar|docking bay]]<ref name="Head to Head">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Head to Head]]''</ref> located in the heart of a small outpost informally known as "[[Jhothal]],"<ref name="Empire Day Trivia Gallery" /> both of which were named after the facility's owner, an [[Ithorian]] named [[Jho]].<ref name="Old Jho's Pit Stop" /><ref name="Epic Battles">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Visual Guide: Epic Battles]]''</ref> Located [[Standard hour|hours]] from [[Capital City]],<ref name="Lothal" /> the Pit Stop's main attraction was a<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> quaint<ref name="Epic Battles" /> [[cantina]] where Old Jho served drinks,<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> popular with locals and travelers alike,<ref name="Old Jho's Pit Stop" /> beneath which was a storeroom.<ref name="The Secret Academy">''[[Servants of the Empire: The Secret Academy]]''</ref> A [[holoprojector]] was mounted on the wall behind the bar.<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> Jho kept his antiquated [[Jho's freight hauler|hauler]] beneath a tarp behind the Pit Stop.<ref name="The Secret Academy" /> Although a very friendly bar owner, the Ithorian kept a [[hunting blaster]] under the counter in case of troublemakers.<ref name="Epic Battles" />

Many of Jho's furnishing were made from repurposed goods, such as lamps built from [[DUM-series pit droid|pit droids]] and an overhead fan made out of a [[gunship]] [[engine]], as well as repurposed [[moisture vaporator]] tanks. Scavenged relics from the [[Clone Wars]] were scattered around the bar to remind patrons of [[the galaxy]]'s wartime history, including a [[Phase I clone trooper armor|Phase I]] [[clone trooper]] helmet<ref name="Epic Battles" /> on a shelf behind the bar<ref name="Empire Day">{{Rebels|Empire Day (episode)}}</ref> and what appeared to be the nose of a [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|Low Altitude Assault Transport]] known as the ''[[Crumb Bomber]]'', which Jho claimed was authentic,<ref name="Empire Day Trivia Gallery" /> was mounted above its hangar bay entrance.<ref name="Empire Day" /> The repair facility's signage, written in a combination of [[Outer Rim Basic]] and [[Aurebesh]], was featured on a pair of LAAT/i wings attached on either side of the gunship's nose.<ref name="Empire Day Concept Art Gallery">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/empire-day-concept-art-gallery|text="Empire Day" Concept Art Gallery}}</ref>

The Pit Stop was said to be the only place on Lothal where one could enjoy refreshments while their vehicle's [[power converter]]s were being changed. Unlike some, Jho did not discriminate, and as long as one had [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] to spare, he would serve whatever a customer wanted, which included [[human]]s, [[humanoid]]s, and even [[droid]]s, whether it was [[Blue milk|bantha milk]] or [[Lubricant|lubricator fluid]].<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> However, Old Jho's Pit Stop was not particularly [[Galactic Empire|Empire]]-friendly, ignoring an Imperial mandate that the [[HoloNet News]] be played at all times.<ref name="Old Jho's Pit Stop" /> Despite this, [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|TIE fighter pilots]] and other Imperials could still be found there.<ref name="Lothal" /> The Pit stop offered a discreet meeting place to [[smuggler]]s, [[Gambling|gamblers]], and the occasional Imperial.<ref name="Epic Battles" />

Jho served simple meals and drinks<ref name="Epic Battles" /> such as [[Lothal Spicebrew|spicebrew]], [[Water|ice-cold]] [[fizzy]],<ref name="Ezra's Duel with Danger" /> and ice water,<ref name="The Secret Academy" /> as well as desserts such as [[space waffle]]s with [[muja sauce]], minced [[Loth-rat pie]], [[Jogan fruit|jogan]] [[Jogan fruitcake|fruitcake]], [[blue milk custard]], and spiced [[nysillin]] [[tea]].<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> After Jho was executed for aiding the Rebellion in [[1 BBY]], the bar was taken over by [[Baron of the Empire|Baron]] [[Valen Rudor]], who turned it into a haunt popular with Imperial personnel.<ref name="The Occupation" />

==History==
In 1 BBY, Jho was executed for attempting to help suspected members of a rebel cell. His bar was seized by the Empire, and given to Baron Valen Rudor, who converted the cantina into a place that was popular among Imperial personnel. While eluding Imperial forces, [[Ezra Bridger]] along with [[Sabine Wren]] visited Jho's former cantina only to learn about Jho's execution. Before Rudor could question the visitors, an old friend [[Jai Kell]] paid for their drinks and escorted them out of the bar, saving the two from being discovered. Kell had already joined [[Ryder Azadi]]'s [[Lothal resistance group]] and led the [[Spectres]] to Ryder's rendezvous point.<ref name="The Occupation" />

Decades later, the diner's logo was used to decorate the [[flight suit]] and [[Green Ace|racing starfighter]] of [[Hype Fazon]], a [[racer]] [[pilot]] on ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Space station|station]].<ref name="Bucket's">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-resistance|text=Designing ''Star Wars'': ''Star Wars Resistance''|date=2018-10-29}} {{C|Slides 6 — 7}}</ref>

